 'The name of this surah is “al-Anfal”, taken from the very first verse of this surah. Anfal is the plural of nafl. Nafl really means an extra thing. The spoils of war are called nafl because they are in excess of the real aim. The real aim of jihad is the reward of the Hereafter and the pleasure of Allah. The coming of the wealth (…) is Allah’s bounty and gift, which is why the spoils of war are called anfal. In this surah the rulings on the distribution of the spoils of war were revealed; it is in this connection that this surah has been named “al-Anfal”.',
